    "narrative": "The LawDog lineup is headlined by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who boasts the day\u2019s highest score at 85.99. Facing the struggling Drake, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from a massive 19% SP Skill boost, cementing him as the primary engine for our offense. **Bryce Harper** (80.21) remains a mandatory start, as a favorable matchup against Baz and a significant 16% park factor uplift push him into elite territory. We are also leaning heavily into our speed-dependent depth today; **Tyler Freeman** (68.73) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (64.44) both provide high-floor value despite facing Buehler. While **Tyler Freeman** battles a poor batting order spot, his ability to exploit Avila\u2019s weak pitching profile keeps him as a strong recommendation for today\u2019s 5x5 rotation.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **JJ Bleday**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a score of 39.81. While **JJ Bleday**\u2019s base projections were respectable, a 15% SP Skill penalty against Ashcraft combined with a significant platoon disadvantage pushed him just below our 40-point \"Zebras\" floor. Consequently, he remains on the bench to preserve our limited game caps. Meanwhile, we are monitoring **Yainer Diaz** (42.39) and **Daulton Varsho** (43.00) closely; both are currently bordering on marginal plays. **Yainer Diaz** is facing a particularly daunting task against deGrom, whose 3.08 xERA presents a significant risk to our daily efficiency. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding our stolen base targets. **Masyn Winn** is positioned well to capitalize on Gausman\u2019s delivery speed, carrying a 52.15 score that reflects his utility in a tight contest. While the rest of the roster, including **Cal Raleigh**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Lawrence Butler**, **Drew Gilbert**, and **Kyle Karros**, are locked into active slots, any late-breaking weather patterns or unexpected lineup shuffles\u2014particularly regarding the lower-scoring bench candidates like **Braden Montgomery**\u2014will necessitate an immediate reassessment of our daily cap exposure.",
